  "query_preview": "..\nAs of 254 PM EDT Thursday...\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Upper level trough and low pressure will remain\nover our region through Saturday. Scattered afternoon showers\nare expected each day, varying in intensity based on potency of\nshortwaves passing through. Tricky to time which day will have\nthe best chance for showers, but presently looks like Saturday\nmay have the most showers. Sunday will trend drier as upper\nlevel trough finally slides eastward and away from our area.\nTemperatures will be a bit cooler than seasonal normals through\nthe weekend.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2: Deep layer ridging will make a brief appearance \non Monday bringing sunshine, light winds, and seasonal \ntemperatures to the North Country and northern New York. This \nperiod of dry weather will be short-lived as a shortwave trough \nin the northwesterly flow aloft flattens the longwave ridge and \ndrives a cold front through the region Monday night into Tuesday\nmorning. This should spark a few showers but no thunderstorms \nor impactful weather are expected with this system as we will \nseriously lack deep moisture. Thereafter, a series of low \namplitude shortwaves are expected to move across the region \nthrough the second half of the work week. Periods of light \nshowers seem plausible through much of the week with ample \nperiod of dry weather between rounds of showers. However, if you\nare looking for an extended period of dry weather, next week \ndoes not look favorable for that at this time.",
